/-!
# The ATLAS matrix model of the fourth Janko group

`TauCeti.Sporadic.J4` is the subgroup of `GL (Fin 112) (ZMod 2)` generated by the two matrices
`J4.a` and `J4.b` of the ATLAS representation `J4G1-f2r112B0`, the images of the type I standard
generators of `J₄` in its representation of dimension `112` over the field with two elements. The
entry in row `i` and column `j` of each matrix is the entry in row `i + 1` and column `j + 1` of
the ATLAS file, and the product is the matrix product, which is also the product in which the
ATLAS programs and the presentation are written.

The presentation selected for `J₄` (`TauCeti.Sporadic.j4Presentation`) is on the type II standard
generators `x`, `y` and `t`, of orders `2`, `3` and `2`, with twelve relators, so the generators of
the model are not such a family. This file gives three matrices `J4.imageX`, `J4.imageY` and
`J4.imageT` in the model that satisfy all twelve relators and generate exactly the model, and
deduces that the presented group `SporadicName.J4.Group` maps onto the model. In particular the
presented group is nontrivial.

Each of the five matrices is given by its table of entries, so that the relators compute directly.
The words `J4.imageX_eq`, `J4.imageY_eq` and `J4.imageT_eq` write the three images in the
generators of the model, which puts them in the model; conversely `J4.a_eq` and `J4.b_eq` write
the generators of the model in the three images, so the images generate the whole model.

The three images were computed from the two generators by the ATLAS program `J4G1-G2W1`, which
converts type I into type II standard generators. For `x` and `y` the words proved here are those
of that program, with its powers and inverses expanded and then shortened by `a² = 1` and
`b⁴ = 1`. The program's word for `t` has more than seventeen thousand letters, and the ATLAS gives
no program in the other direction; the words for `t`, `a` and `b` proved here were found by
computer instead, by a search through the conjugates of an involution and, for `b`, through the
centralizer of `t`. Nothing about these computations is used, and that `J4.imageT` is the output
of the program is not asserted: the relators and both directions of generation are checked here.

All computations run on the packed matrices of `TauCeti.BitMatrix`, whose product the kernel
evaluates in `112` steps on natural numbers. Each of the five matrices is the image under
`TauCeti.BitMatrix.toGL` of an invertible packed matrix (`J4.packedA`, `J4.packedB`, `J4.packedX`,
`J4.packedY`, `J4.packedT`), and an equation between words is decided on the packed side.

No order of the model or of the presented group is asserted here, and the surjection is not shown
to be injective.

The lift and range arguments use `GroupPresentation.homEquiv` and
`GroupPresentation.exists_surjective_of_closure_range_eq`.

## Main declarations

* `TauCeti.Sporadic.J4`: the matrix model, generated by `TauCeti.Sporadic.J4.a` and
  `TauCeti.Sporadic.J4.b`.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.J4.imageX`, `TauCeti.Sporadic.J4.imageY`, `TauCeti.Sporadic.J4.imageT`: the
  images of the three generators, with `TauCeti.Sporadic.J4.presentationImage` the resulting
  assignment.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.J4.lift_presentationImage_toFreeGroup_eq_one`: the twelve relators hold.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.J4.closure_range_presentationImage`: the images generate the model.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.J4.presentationHom`, `TauCeti.Sporadic.J4.range_presentationHom`: the
  homomorphism from the presented group and its range.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.exists_surjective_J4`: the presented group maps onto the model.

## References

* R. A. Wilson, R. A. Parker, J. N. Bray et al., *ATLAS of Finite Group Representations*,
  version 3, representation `J4G1-f2r112B0`,
  <https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/v3/matrep/J4G1-f2r112B0>. Matrix files:
  <https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/spor/J4/mtx/J4G1-f2r112B0.m1> and
  <https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/spor/J4/mtx/J4G1-f2r112B0.m2>. Program from the type I
  to the type II standard generators:
  <https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/spor/J4/words/J4G1-G2W1>.
* S. W. Bolt, J. N. Bray, and R. T. Curtis, *Symmetric presentation of the Janko group J₄*,
  Journal of the London Mathematical Society **76** (2007), 683--701,
  <https://doi.org/10.1112/jlms/jdm086>, for the presentation.
-/

